## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* the live hash moved during the gate; the pre-copy missing, changed or not executable; any difference from the pre-copy other than line 84 and the 5 comment lines; a `KK_T9` string left; the default string not exact; an unset variable NOT landing under the default, or a set variable not winning, or an empty variable not falling back; FIFO arms 1-7 red on the live copy while green on the pre-copy; a caller shape failing on the live copy but passing on the pre-copy; the probe not acquiring on `locks-laptop-1017`, or any `/Volumes/KK_T9*` created, or the probe's records not appearing; non-ASCII, a person name or a decision-card id in the added lines; any entry under `session-tools/` changed that the builder did not declare and no other seat explains; a new `.new-847` leftover. *Major (class named on the line, "NO GO 1 of 2"):* a surviving mutant G-M1 to G-M6 (the arms do not hold the value, the override, the fallback or the absolute path); a builder claim contradicted by your measurement that changes the basis (a hash, the count of changed lines, the arms 1-7 results, the probe's records); a census finding that a live caller passes a base other than `locks-laptop-1017`. *Minor/Note:* the other tools that still name the T9; the live file's mtime older than the swap; the missing-volume residual risk; the harness noise the builder lists (`tree.pids` message, arm 6 `runs=14` against the records' 16); the stale `locks/` directory; kits still pinning the old hash; the ticket key in the header comment; `ls` date-format oddities.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1-6 measured with their controls, Check 5 completed, the live hash equal at all four reads. A NO GO names the class and "round 1 of 2" and gives the fix-shape in prose; a finding that asks for a redesign (a missing-volume guard, a derived default, removing the explicit variable from the kits) is a ruling for the product owner, never a defect of this change. **A NO GO is NOT followed by any action of yours:** the pre-copy stays, you do not run the rollback; Tuesday decides and runs the builder kit's own recipe (quoted by you in FOR TUESDAY). **STOP (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <the change and why>`) if** the live hash moved, `.new-847` appears, a `KK_T9*` volume mounts, a request leaves loopback, or a security-shaped finding you cannot classify.
**First line of STATUS (the verdict line; at Step 0 the placeholder `GATE VERDICT B706: PENDING`):** `GATE VERDICT B706: nexusai-lock.sh <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ sha256 cf01bafb (round 1 of 2 on class "the NexusAI lock tool's default base" - text <1 non-comment line changed y/n; 5 comment lines y/n; rest byte-equal y/n; KK_T9 0 y/n; default string exact y/n> - hashes <live cf01bafb y/n at 4 reads; pre-copy 3c33f5ae y/n; mode y/n; .new-847 absent y/n> - mechanics <unset A y/n; empty A y/n; set wins y/n; control B y/n> - arms <FIFO 1-7 pre PASS n/7 live PASS n/7; A1-A9 n of 9; shapes n of 5; interop y/n> - mutants <k of 6 as predicted; survivors n> - probe <acquired y/n after n s; released +2 y/n; KK_T9 created n; NOT TESTED if so> - census <callers n; other base values n; no-variable callers n; T9-naming tools n> - session-tools census <only declared entries y/n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS, instrument and load, Checks 1-6 each with the FAIL clock and the evidence path, the arms table (arm, pre-copy, live copy), the mutant matrix, the builder-claims table (claim, your number, agree y/n), FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words with the class and round; the sha256 the verdict is valid for; the kits and REFUSE lines that pin `3c33f5ae` and need restamping with `cf01bafb` before any NexusAI seat launches, B703 first; the builder's rollback recipe as text; the records seat moves RD-847 and the C-63-style follow-up line, not the gate), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B706 nexusai-lock.sh sha256 cf01bafb <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on class "the NexusAI lock tool's default base"` (the line carries none of the words that name a landing, a swap or an undo; the findings ids with severities and classes sit on the line above it), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
**HOLD (Tuesday's, restated by you, done by you never).** After a GO or GO WITH FINDINGS: Tuesday restamps every kit that pins the old hash, then launches the next NexusAI build seat. After a NO GO: Tuesday decides the undo by the builder kit's recipe. This gate does none of it.
